"content_hash":"64ba2890bb723b9b0e00a956e2e0040670e7667924c686c6a6312cd9e7b131f9","event_uuid":"1343b5c3-935a-42fd-95c0-338a2b676316","position":{"commit_sha":"386f02e1928e7dcabf57a2e11e64635c973d9779","position":"1788578209909364001-1343b5c3-935a-42fd-95c0-338a2b676316"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Claimed; beginning held-out TDD in worktree janitor-3a46-32f3.","timestamp":1788567161759079001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788314723811551001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f2bb6ac6-f8c3-403e-8701-ac857c2a8d95","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"8eff-87c1-d09a-4893"},{"link_uuid":"a715c3f1-04f8-439d-afef-64508ae527ec","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0620-c33a-487a-4ec1"},{"link_uuid":"882cd193-ece5-4f05-a49e-f11c7bfc30a6","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5ee1-b5c3-2681-49ce"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nPrivate compatibility aliases remain for CLI help routing, `run_security_detectors`, graph/reducer symbols, split reducer processors, and grounding `DIMENSIONS`. Their consumers are internal source or test/monkeypatch paths; no public wire or persisted-data contract requires them. The governing ADR is delivered by earthen-wheat-chick.\n\n## Approach\n\nAfter the ADR merges, migrate all consumers to `_help_route`, `run_detectors`, graph loader/reducer canonical owners, split reducer processor modules, and `grounding.oracle.DIMENSIONS`. Delete old aliases only when both semantic references and raw dynamic/string/monkeypatch census are empty.\n\n## Scope\n\n- CLI help aliases\n- code-review detector, graph/reducer, and grounding compatibility bindings\n- every source/test/patch/dynamic consumer\n\n## Testing\n\nRun targeted CLI/help, security-detector, graph/reducer, and grounding suites plus semantic and raw reference censuses.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Each listed old private name is absent after all consumers migrate to its named canonical owner.\n- [x] Tests patch or import only canonical owners.\n- [x] Public CLI behavior, security detector results, graph reduction, reducer events, and grounding dimensions remain unchanged.\n- [x] Focused suites and complete semantic/raw reference scans pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","reason":"remove private help forwarding aliases"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py","reason":"canonical CLI help owner"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/detectors.py","reason":"remove run_security_detectors shim"},{"path":"src/rebar/graph","reason":"remove graph reducer compatibility bindings and migrate graph loader patch points in the current graph package"},{"path":"src/rebar/reducer","reason":"migrate processor compatibility exports to split canonical owners"},{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/detectors/__init__.py","reason":"remove package-level DIMENSIONS re-export that mirrored registry.DIMENSIONS"},{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/detectors/registry.py","reason":"remove DIMENSIONS re-export"},{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/oracle.py","reason":"canonical DIMENSIONS owner"},{"path":"tests","reason":"migrate every test, string, and monkeypatch consumer"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","8eff-87c1-d09a-4893"],["parent","6640-ac11-5c55-46b5"],["relates_to","0620-c33a-487a-4ec1"],["relates_to","5ee1-b5c3-2681-49ce"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"6640-ac11-5c